        <headline>SYSTEMS BLEED AND PRESSURISATION DAILY REVIEW</headline>
        <description>BACKGROUND: A REVIEW OF ACMS DATA SHOWS RH BLEED PRECOOLER OUTLET TEMPERATURE TRENDING HIGH AND BLEED PX IN CLIMB. THIS WORK ORDER HAS BEEN RAISED TO TROUBLESHOOT.

ACTION:

1). OBSERVING ALL SAFETY PRECAUTIONS, GAIN ACCESS TO THE AIRCRAFT.

2). USING PNEUMATIC TESTING KIT (P/N 1945-04-08) PERFORM A COMPLETE PNEUMATIC HEALTH CHECK OF #2 BLEED COMPONENTS IAW AMM 36-11-00.

*RECORD THE RESULTS ON THE RA851 FORM AND SUBMIT TO BLEEDREVIEW@RYANAIR.COM

** RECORD THE SERIAL NUMBER OF THE TEST KIT USED ON THE RA851.

3). LEAK CHECK ALL HSR / HSV / PCCV / BAR SENSE LINES USING SUITABLE LEAK CHECK SPRAY. SPECIAL FOCUS ON  THE FOLLOWING SENSE LINES OR FITTINGS:
    A) PRSOV DOWNSTREAM PRESSURE SENSE LINE
    B) SENSE LINES BETWEEN BAR AND PCCV
    C) SUPPLY SENSE LINE TO HSR
    D) SENSE LINE TO PRSOV
    E) SENSE LINE TO 450 SENSOR
    F) 390 SENSOR SENSE LINES FROM PCCV UNION
    G) SENSE LINE BETWEEN HSR AND HSV

4). INSPECT THE #2 PCCV KISS SEAL IAW AMM 36-12-02. REPLACE IF NECESSARY.

5). CHECK INSTALLATION OF PRECOOLER SENSE LINE 332A2350-14 WITH REFERENCE TO AMM TASK 36-12-02-400-801 PRECOOLER CONTROL VALVE INSTALLATION.  

NOTE: ADJUST THE PRESSURE SENSE LINES TO MAKE SURE THAT THERE IS NO PRELOAD ON THE LINES, OR UNION FITTINGS. PRELOAD CAN CAUSE DAMAGE TO THE LINES.

6). REPLACE THE #2 PCCV IAW AMM 36-12-02/401.

7). RETURN THE AIRCRAFT TO SERVICEABLE CONDITION.

** AIRCRAFT IS EQUIPPED WITH ACMS - NO BLEED SHEETS WILL BE REQUIRED.

** PLEASE ENSURE THE ALL ELECTRIC AND PNEUMATIC FITTINGS/COMPONENTS DISTURBED DURING THE ABOVE WORKS ARE RE-INSTATED TO CORRECT CONFIGURATION BEFORE AIRCRAFT IS RETURNED TO SERVICE.</description>
